From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: the full-grab tap at the end of the chain for keyboard sharing apps

What: with OMACVM_KEYS_LAST=1 the full-grab event tap goes at the end of
macOS's event tap chain (kCGTailAppendEventTap) instead of its head.
OmacVM.app sets it for a start when its hidden setting is on:
  defaults write org.omacvm.app shareKeyboard -bool true
qemu.log then says "full-grab tap at the end of the event tap chain".
Without it nothing changes. OmacVM Gestures and the Bridge read the same
setting for their own taps.

Why: issue #350. A keyboard sharing app (Synergy, Deskflow, Barrier, Input
Leap) taps the keys at the head of the HID chain too, and the newest tap
runs first. A VM started after the sharing app took the keys while the
pointer was on the other computer. At the end of the chain the sharing app
sees the keys first: it keeps those it sends to the other computer, the VM
gets the rest. The escape combo still passes (omacvm-cocoa-escape-combo-
tap.patch), so the tap order with OmacVM Gestures does not matter.

Upstream: not sent (OmacVM's setting).

Test: app/runtime/Tests/keys/test-keys-last.sh (CI: omacvm_keys_place from
this patch with OMACVM_KEYS_LAST unset, 1, 0 and other values; the runtime
build: the same from the patched ui/cocoa.m, and that the tap is made at
that place). Applies after omacvm-cocoa-tap-permission.patch, before
omacvm-cocoa-no-app-nap.patch (last).

diff --git a/ui/cocoa.m b/ui/cocoa.m
--- a/ui/cocoa.m
+++ b/ui/cocoa.m
@@ -1891,12 +1891,29 @@
     }
 }
 
+/*
+ * OmacVM (#350): where the full-grab tap goes in macOS's event tap chain.
+ * A keyboard sharing app (Synergy, Deskflow, Barrier, Input Leap) taps the
+ * keys at the head of the chain too, and the newest tap runs first: a VM
+ * started after it took the keys while the pointer was on the other
+ * computer. With OMACVM_KEYS_LAST=1 (OmacVM.app's hidden shareKeyboard
+ * setting) the tap goes at the end, so the sharing app sees the keys first.
+ * Without it: at the head, as before.
+ */
+static CGEventTapPlacement omacvm_keys_place(void)
+{
+    const char *v = getenv("OMACVM_KEYS_LAST");
+
+    return v && !strcmp(v, "1") ? kCGTailAppendEventTap : kCGHeadInsertEventTap;
+}
+
 - (void) setFullGrab:(id)sender
 {
     COCOA_DEBUG("QemuCocoaView: setFullGrab\n");
 
     CGEventMask mask = CGEventMaskBit(kCGEventKeyDown) | CGEventMaskBit(kCGEventKeyUp) | CGEventMaskBit(kCGEventFlagsChanged);
-    eventsTap = CGEventTapCreate(kCGHIDEventTap, kCGHeadInsertEventTap, kCGEventTapOptionDefault,
+    CGEventTapPlacement place = omacvm_keys_place();
+    eventsTap = CGEventTapCreate(kCGHIDEventTap, place, kCGEventTapOptionDefault,
                                  mask, handleTapEvent, self);
     if (!eventsTap) {
         warn_report("Could not create event tap, system key combos will not be captured.\n");
@@ -1904,6 +1921,10 @@
     } else {
         COCOA_DEBUG("Global events tap created! Will capture system key combos.\n");
     }
+    if (place == kCGTailAppendEventTap) {
+        info_report("cocoa: full-grab tap at the end of the event tap chain "
+                    "(OMACVM_KEYS_LAST=1: keyboard sharing apps see the keys first)");
+    }
 
     CFRunLoopRef runLoop = CFRunLoopGetCurrent();
     if (!runLoop) {
